    {
      "id": "IRW-02",
      "title": "Hermitian duality lifts every admissible row when f≥2e",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-inert-row-lift",
      "statement": "For every admissible row r, the paired column b is its negative reversed conjugate. Set b₁=CVg b, b₂=CU b and use the Hermitian form H(x,y)=Σσ(xᵢ)y_rev(i). For any integral τ of trace one, c=r·b₁+τ(H(b₁,b₁)−H(b₂,b₂)) has trace r·b, and ϖ^f(c−r·b₁) is integral if f≥2e. These data give an element of the unitary radical with the prescribed row and corrected corner bound.",
