      "id": "IRW-03",
      "title": "A dyadic row attaining the quadratic denominator cost",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-inert-row-example",
      "statement": "For L=ℚ₂(ω), ω²+ω+1=0, the rank-one middle block with g=C=U=1,V=0 has four classes of rows at e=1. For r=1/2 the formula gives c=ω/4 with τ=−ω. The case a=1,j=0 supplies exactly f=2. With f=1 no corner can satisfy both the unitary trace and the denominator condition for this row.",
